# J137: Synergy v2 against the designed v3

Compare folder: `var/lab-j137/compare`; 1500 and 1500 drafts on the same seeds (compare asserts it). Pairs count with 40+ decisive games. Wilson intervals carry the study's design effect 1.25 (the plain Wilson interval beside it).

## The pre-registered rule (synergy-v3-design.md §4, written 2026-10-16 before any v3 draft)

v3 is **BETTER BALANCED** iff v3's pair-spread 95% interval lies wholly below v2's (v3's upper bound < v2's lower bound) AND no v3 pair with 40+ decisive games has a Wilson 95% interval wholly below 35%. Anything else is **NOT SHOWN**, never "no change". A pass ships nothing: Justin decides.

| cube | pair spread | 95% interval (compare's paired draft-clustered bootstrap) | pairs counted |
|---|---|---|---|
| v2 | 38.9 | [33.7, 44.3] | 10 |
| v3 | 27.1 | [20.8, 35.1] | 10 |

- Spread: v3's upper 35.1 is not below v2's lower 33.7.
- Pairs: no v3 pair wholly below 35%.
- Paired difference v2 − v3 (description only): 11.8 [3.2, 19.5].

**Verdict: NOT SHOWN.**

